&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="redirect"&gt;&lt;code&gt;redirect&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="redirect"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#redirect" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The rule applied before a token, a key set or a signed assertion crosses a
link: &lt;strong&gt;the URL is https, or it names this machine.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-go" data-lang="go"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;github.com/go-authn/harden/redirect&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;http&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Timeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Second&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;CheckRedirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;CheckRedirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;HTTPSOrLoopback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;issuer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Function&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;CheckRedirect(req, via) error&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an &lt;code&gt;http.Client&lt;/code&gt; policy: stops after 10 redirects and refuses a target that is not https and not loopback (https to http on another host is the case it exists for). Chain your own policy after it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;HTTPSOrLoopback(rawURL) error&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;nil for &lt;code&gt;https://host.example/...&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;http://&lt;/code&gt; with a loopback host. Refuses no host, other schemes and cleartext. The error names the scheme and host, never the whole URL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Loopback(host) bool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;host&lt;/code&gt; as &lt;code&gt;url.URL.Hostname()&lt;/code&gt; returns it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Loopback&lt;/code&gt; accepts an IP literal that is loopback (127.0.0.0/8, &lt;code&gt;::1&lt;/code&gt;,IPv4-mapped &lt;code&gt;::ffff:127.0.0.1&lt;/code&gt;), and &lt;code&gt;localhost&lt;/code&gt; or any name under&lt;code&gt;.localhost&lt;/code&gt; (RFC 6761 section 6.3), in any letter case, with or without the
trailing dot. It never matches a prefix, so &lt;code&gt;127.evil.example&lt;/code&gt; is refused, as
are &lt;code&gt;0x7f.1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;127.1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;2130706433&lt;/code&gt;, an IPv6 zone and the bracketed &lt;code&gt;[::1]&lt;/code&gt;
(brackets are URL syntax, not part of a host).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Loopback&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;HTTPSOrLoopback&lt;/code&gt; are fuzzed against a second reading of the
RFC; the corpus is committed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is what &lt;a href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/oidc/"&gt;oidc&lt;/a&gt; (v0.8.1),&lt;a href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/saml/"&gt;saml&lt;/a&gt; (v0.7.3),&lt;a href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/wireguard/"&gt;wireguard&lt;/a&gt;, rp (v0.5.1) and awscred(v0.3.1) apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="privfile"&gt;&lt;code&gt;privfile&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="privfile"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#privfile" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-go" data-lang="go"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;github.com/go-authn/harden/privfile&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;privfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Write&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ticket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Write&lt;/code&gt; puts data at &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; with mode 0600: a temporary file in the same
directory, &lt;code&gt;fsync&lt;/code&gt;, then &lt;code&gt;rename&lt;/code&gt;. So:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a reader sees the old file or the new one, never half of one;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a symbolic link left at &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;replaced, not followed&lt;/strong&gt; (what it pointed
at is untouched), and a file of looser mode does not keep its mode;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;on Unix, a directory that is a symbolic link, belongs to someone else or is
writable by group or others is refused before anything is written.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It does not create the directory. On Windows there is no mode to read; since
v0.2.0 the file is made with a protected access list holding one entry, the
current account, set by &lt;code&gt;CreateFile&lt;/code&gt; (kinit v0.3.2&amp;rsquo;s list), so the folder&amp;rsquo;s
entries are never inherited. The module requires &lt;code&gt;golang.org/x/sys&lt;/code&gt;, used by
Windows builds only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is what writes kinit&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;--cred-file&lt;/code&gt; (v0.3.3), wireguard&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;FloorFile&lt;/code&gt;
(v0.2.1), &lt;code&gt;authn-revokd&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s state file (revocation v0.7.2) and&lt;a href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/secretsource/"&gt;secretsource&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s KeePassXC
association file (v0.8.1).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="floors"&gt;Floors&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="floors"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#floors" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;go-authn/wireguard and go-authn/revocation both keep an ordering floor across a
restart, but they do not share a floor: wireguard keeps a bare version and issue
time in a small file of its own, revocation keeps the whole signed list and
recomputes the floor by verifying it. Only the file write is common, and that
is &lt;code&gt;privfile&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="memlock"&gt;&lt;code&gt;memlock&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="memlock"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#memlock" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since v0.3.0 (moved from theca): keep key material out of swap, and out of core
files and debuggers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-go" data-lang="go"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;github.com/go-authn/harden/memlock&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;region&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;memlock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Lock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unsafe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Pointer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]),&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;uintptr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;len&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// refused: say so, or stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;defer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;region&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Release&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Function&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Lock(p, n) (*Region, error)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;locks the pages of the range with &lt;code&gt;mlock&lt;/code&gt; (Linux, macOS, the BSDs) or &lt;code&gt;VirtualLock&lt;/code&gt; (Windows). &lt;strong&gt;A refusal is an error&lt;/strong&gt;: nothing stays locked and the caller decides. Pages shared by two regions stay locked until both are released&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(*Locker).LockBestEffort(p, n, report)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the same, but each refusal goes to &lt;code&gt;report&lt;/code&gt; and the rest still locks. The name says it: use it only where running unlocked is acceptable&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(*Region).Release()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;unlocks; safe on nil and when called twice&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;DisableDumps() error&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;RLIMIT_CORE&lt;/code&gt; to 0 and, on Linux, &lt;code&gt;PR_SET_DUMPABLE&lt;/code&gt; to 0; on macOS only, &lt;code&gt;PT_DENY_ATTACH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Any other platform gets an &lt;code&gt;*UnsupportedError&lt;/code&gt; (it matches&lt;code&gt;errors.ErrUnsupported&lt;/code&gt;), never a silent success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It guarantees&lt;/strong&gt; that the pages of the range are locked in memory from &lt;code&gt;Lock&lt;/code&gt;
to &lt;code&gt;Release&lt;/code&gt;, or that you got an error. &lt;strong&gt;It does not guarantee&lt;/strong&gt; that no copy
exists: the Go garbage collector can copy a heap object before it is locked, so
lock memory that does not move, and keep the secret in one place. The system
limits still apply (&lt;code&gt;RLIMIT_MEMLOCK&lt;/code&gt;; on Windows, the working-set size).Windows has no equivalent of &lt;code&gt;PR_SET_DUMPABLE&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;PT_DENY_ATTACH&lt;/code&gt;: a debugger
of the same user or an administrator can read the process.&lt;/p&gt;
